---
import Step from "./Step.astro"
---

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>Three steps. Nothing to run.</h2>
    <ol>
      <Step title="Pick a change" example={{ kind: "command", text: "trek main...HEAD ../gateway" }}>
        A git range or pull requests, across one or more repos — or work not yet committed.
      </Step>
      <Step
        title="Your agent builds the trek"
        example={{ kind: "prompt", text: "Build a trek of this branch." }}
      >
        Register <code>trek mcp</code> with your agent. It reads the change at its exact revisions and
        follows one example scenario from trigger to outcome.
      </Step>
      <Step title="Step through it" example={{ kind: "command", text: ":Trek pay" }}>
        In Neovim or VS Code: next and previous in execution order, step over, into, and out, with
        the narration and call stack for each stop.
      </Step>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    ol {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* The route's colours, start to end. */
  ol > :global(li:nth-child(1)) {
    --step-color: var(--indigo);
  }

  ol > :global(li:nth-child(2)) {
    --step-color: var(--cyan);
  }

  ol > :global(li:nth-child(3)) {
    --step-color: var(--gold);
  }
</style>
